d "b1e12b5e-f23d-52bf-b80e-0e49a813bd26" :question/math-academy-id "q-70828" :question/problem "A nonzero vector $⟨0,\\,b,c⟩$ is parallel to the plane $r\\cdot ⟨-2,2,-4⟩=15.$ What is the value of $\\frac{b}{c}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need a vector $v=⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩$ that is parallel to the given plane. \n\nFrom the equation $r\\cdot ⟨-2,2,-4⟩=15$ of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨-2,2,-4⟩.$ So, $v⊥n$ and we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ ⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,2,-4⟩ & =0 \\\\ -2{t}_{1}+2{t}_{2}-4{t}_{3} & =0 \\\\ 2{t}_{2} & =2{t}_{1}+4{t}_{3} \\\\ {t}_{2} & ={t}_{1}+2{t}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain \n\n$$\nv=⟨{t}_{1},\\,{t}_{1}+2{t}_{3},\\,{t}_{3}⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere ${t}_{1},{t}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nWe are told that the first component of $v$ equals $0.$ So, we must set ${t}_{1}=0.$ \n\nSince $v$ is nonzero, we can pick any ${t}_{3}\\ne 0.$ For example, setting ${t}_{3}=1$, we get\n\n$$\nv=⟨0,\\,2,\\,1⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{b}{c}=2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-70828/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0d93156-f9be-5e6e-976a-bef30dc892ee"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-70828"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-70830/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "1c2cc8a9-e28e-533f-bf7f-0f459cb5cdf7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70830/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "f78e0115-2e16-50ae-9c52-760c00875cee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70830/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "ff90f966-b127-5050-a0e2-f4bbf9689b53" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70830/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "7de622e4-1179-559d-9868-86fed7a9a2c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70830/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "4fd3b7b9-c00f-5e23-a56d-49f5c06e2136" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70830/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "78f8e23e-90e1-5a1e-b028-398ee1e15492" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-70830/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-70830/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" "q-70830/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-70830/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-70830/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-70830/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-70830" :question/id #uuid "16749763-ce77-5654-ad19-901c646ee9ee" :question/math-academy-id "q-70830" :question/problem "A nonzero vector $⟨a,\\,b,\\,0⟩$ is parallel to the plane $r\\cdot ⟨-1,1,-3⟩=8.$ What is the value of $\\frac{a}{b}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need a vector $v=⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩$ that is parallel to the given plane. \n\nFrom the equation $r\\cdot ⟨-1,1,-3⟩=8$ of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨-1,1,-3⟩.$ So, $v⊥n$ and we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ ⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩\\cdot ⟨-1,1,-3⟩ & =0 \\\\ -{t}_{1}+{t}_{2}-3{t}_{3} & =0 \\\\ {t}_{2} & ={t}_{1}+3{t}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain \n\n$$\nv=⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{1}+3{t}_{3},{t}_{3}⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere ${t}_{1},{t}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nWe are told that the third component of $v$ equals $0.$ So, we must set ${t}_{3}=0.$ \n\nSince $v$ is nonzero, we can pick any ${t}_{1}\\ne 0.$ For example, setting ${t}_{1}=1$, we get\n\n$$\nv=⟨1,\\,1,\\,0⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{a}{b}=1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-70830/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0d93156-f9be-5e6e-976a-bef30dc892ee"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-70830"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-127937/selection/f27c19c1355462a0f5baea028169e16edd67bc2bccc2ddc9a2332fa07e1f5940" :answer/id #uuid "88e38b3b-d0e0-5930-b8b9-dd2485c127b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨2,6,2⟩=12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127937/selection/a62722153064e2c9cd12ffd47ba0df19c261f6724311265c2e0975b5d2b2e059" :answer/id #uuid "013eae6a-093f-5868-8fc4-0d2b8abb0040" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨6,2,2⟩=16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127937/selection/bbf818957e62b3b8839a201c7e1752f6138636e7db4a9f752dff8584e2ecc7a5" :answer/id #uuid "7c7607c9-f26a-5689-8932-61774fb7d075" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨3,2,2⟩=8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127937/selection/074c883f0ae7f72add99b72a6ca427328567e7edddef01c82583d62ff3126255" :answer/id #uuid "fc8a9931-4b41-5c66-9d98-fcf79c4820c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨2,2,3⟩=22" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127937/selection/42249331ee8c3bea01d145c44a14ea7e68f015054b1bb2658dcba0f0d46e1503" :answer/id #uuid "347d57a2-fbb7-5583-bb16-786d4e1ae381" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨2,3,2⟩=14" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127937/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3f9ca81e-819f-5a83-8bcc-efef9d6aa0a5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-127937/selection/a62722153064e2c9cd12ffd47ba0df19c261f6724311265c2e0975b5d2b2e059" :answer-field/choices ["q-127937/selection/f27c19c1355462a0f5baea028169e16edd67bc2bccc2ddc9a2332fa07e1f5940" "q-127937/selection/a62722153064e2c9cd12ffd47ba0df19c261f6724311265c2e0975b5d2b2e059" "q-127937/selection/bbf818957e62b3b8839a201c7e1752f6138636e7db4a9f752dff8584e2ecc7a5" "q-127937/selection/074c883f0ae7f72add99b72a6ca427328567e7edddef01c82583d62ff3126255" "q-127937/selection/42249331ee8c3bea01d145c44a14ea7e68f015054b1bb2658dcba0f0d46e1503"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-127937" :question/id #uuid "78e0dc1f-5e12-54f0-b00c-492a979933d2" :question/math-academy-id "q-127937" :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(2,-1,3)$ and is perpendicular to the line that goes through the points \n$A(-4,1,3)$ and $B(2,3,5).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨2,-1,3⟩.$\n\nSince the line  passes through the points $A(-4,1,3)$ and $B(2,3,5)$ we can find a vector parallel to the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨2,3,5⟩-⟨-4,1,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6,2,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨6,2,2⟩.$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-p\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨6,2,2⟩ & =⟨2,-1,3⟩\\cdot ⟨6,2,2⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨6,2,2⟩ & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-127937/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "45cdbb0d-2986-5c05-8d23-dce29363051b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-127937"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-127944/selection/17a829d6e5181d71f62a2ca86fd3de0a25f7fbbe4e386f6cb82ec3901fd99aba" :answer/id #uuid "8d1083a7-8ac3-5e89-9c34-77320f55a409" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-3,4,1⟩=9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127944/selection/d6ce728e8dacce39552d24c7a56f82e16c963fb83539b1f775db6a0cd5fdf00a" :answer/id #uuid "0d17c3cb-71a1-5e7d-bc66-618007380fe9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-4,3,1⟩=7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127944/selection/f0891b1faa1ae5c1271f0102d33c66a225261aec6d2e171268f2faf8d228fa27" :answer/id #uuid "acef90b4-5796-578f-8f57-aaba20ba47ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨3,1,4⟩=13" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127944/selection/8d8cc89c588a057ce79a9f990a571e6b03e71a434b5a025bcb00efa9a7d4b788" :answer/id #uuid "24c06ecf-5904-5987-bbad-17a96f7593f2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,-4,3⟩=15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127944/selection/64e7ac7eb5fb9d37ed6f18973ec9f2a38a76e22c5a83ff97caf00e1ee302b80a" :answer/id #uuid "3eed3c19-8e3e-504d-8d6e-7979b366f1ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,4,3⟩=11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127944/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c8739ff2-6b64-5141-8eae-d81ba06fd6a7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-127944/selection/17a829d6e5181d71f62a2ca86fd3de0a25f7fbbe4e386f6cb82ec3901fd99aba" :answer-field/choices ["q-127944/selection/17a829d6e5181d71f62a2ca86fd3de0a25f7fbbe4e386f6cb82ec3901fd99aba" "q-127944/selection/d6ce728e8dacce39552d24c7a56f82e16c963fb83539b1f775db6a0cd5fdf00a" "q-127944/selection/f0891b1faa1ae5c1271f0102d33c66a225261aec6d2e171268f2faf8d228fa27" "q-127944/selection/8d8cc89c588a057ce79a9f990a571e6b03e71a434b5a025bcb00efa9a7d4b788" "q-127944/selection/64e7ac7eb5fb9d37ed6f18973ec9f2a38a76e22c5a83ff97caf00e1ee302b80a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-127944" :question/id #uuid "47335439-5d39-5166-8bb4-814a188345e9" :question/math-academy-id "q-127944" :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $Q(-1,1,2)$ and is perpendicular to the line \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=5-3t \\\\ y=2+4t \\\\ z=-3+t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vector of $Q$ is $q=⟨-1,1,2⟩.$ Converting the parametric equations of the line to vector form, we get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=5-3t \\\\ y=2+4t \\\\ z=-3+t\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,⟨x,y,z⟩=⟨5,2,-3⟩+t\\text{ }{{⟨-3,4,1⟩}_{⏟}}_{v}.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe direction vector of the line is $v=⟨-3,4,1⟩,$ so a normal vector to the plane is \n\n$$\nn=v=⟨-3,4,1⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-3,4,1⟩ & =⟨-1,1,2⟩\\cdot ⟨-3,4,1⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-3,4,1⟩ & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-127944/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "45cdbb0d-2986-5c05-8d23-dce29363051b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-127944"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-70892/selection/1b35e804947d3a9b32b5e1423d38e5c7fd6a71b2ce89324eaf8df599b8fe1acc" :answer/id #uuid "7c31152e-66dd-5fe9-9562-96be7263d661" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨2,1,-1⟩=⟨1,1,1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70892/selection/d8ca54a6d00d8bbd02ac865b2dc0575ea2991853d69c6529c78322566ebbe458" :answer/id #uuid "7bd83c0d-0368-5584-91e4-39648a268e3b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,1,1⟩=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70892/selection/583a2628651f8d730587cfb510e23ce3d4a67f81acdba076d01f724fc987111b" :answer/id #uuid "4ea2f177-4c47-5d19-aa6d-d0bf73033d47" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,1,1⟩=⟨2,1,-1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70892/selection/96a0f2a1a5016e2187bc24a9cf63e19d9061a991cb59d691711c9d8987857fa0" :answer/id #uuid "e4b58dd1-3b24-551d-b476-8762f33d28b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨2,1,-1⟩=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70892/selection/03cfa7570fcf23c2bd215d8400f39e10a089ce9ed709446d0b05d53f4802af76" :answer/id #uuid "295f1e58-4a16-5d5a-b676-984818a41fed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,1,1⟩=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70892/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "475d5cee-306a-5cd5-b998-795c7327de73" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-70892/selection/03cfa7570fcf23c2bd215d8400f39e10a089ce9ed709446d0b05d53f4802af76" :answer-field/choices ["q-70892/selection/1b35e804947d3a9b32b5e1423d38e5c7fd6a71b2ce89324eaf8df599b8fe1acc" "q-70892/selection/d8ca54a6d00d8bbd02ac865b2dc0575ea2991853d69c6529c78322566ebbe458" "q-70892/selection/583a2628651f8d730587cfb510e23ce3d4a67f81acdba076d01f724fc987111b" "q-70892/selection/96a0f2a1a5016e2187bc24a9cf63e19d9061a991cb59d691711c9d8987857fa0" "q-70892/selection/03cfa7570fcf23c2bd215d8400f39e10a089ce9ed709446d0b05d53f4802af76"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-70892" :question/id #uuid "be607052-6286-5c45-a7b0-2a7d8e65a24b" :question/math-academy-id "q-70892" :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $Q(2,1,-1)$ and is perpendicular to the line that goes through the points \n$A(2,1,0)$ and $B(3,2,1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of $Q$ is $q=⟨2,1,-1⟩.$\n\nSince the line  passes through the points $A(2,1,0)$ and $B(3,2,1)$ we can find a vector parallel to the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨3,2,1⟩-⟨2,1,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,1,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨1,1,1⟩.$ \n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨1,1,1⟩ & =⟨2,1,-1⟩\\cdot ⟨1,1,1⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨1,1,1⟩ & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-70892/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "45cdbb0d-2986-5c05-8d23-dce29363051b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-70892"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-127956/selection/4a259362c2a3e0418034bdb8a360ae2f2074603d64535d40483d48b2648fb2dc" :answer/id #uuid "7cd3a595-2dde-5063-906b-d1b04e1d20b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨4,-2,1⟩=18" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127956/selection/c4eb48c3cb07e7c3471776e0c89ba5f667a5d947317bec956bcc3c68bad1c1d9" :answer/id #uuid "68ff1c28-aac5-52bb-92b7-b6bdc4b84f44" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨-2,2,1⟩=12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127956/selection/30cc1824d522d837a7d3dee93f22b9216bcf782fafd32ca5faf80f1b98e5500f" :answer/id #uuid "b40b62f9-f45d-5d3f-a5cf-678820eea359" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,-2,4⟩=22" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127956/selection/6ce83711a830e5b9a0ac8b7db7cd2faa183875d3ab0d04a2213c2cfcda8d09ab" :answer/id #uuid "1d5d8a0f-8eff-5258-8da6-ac9b0c88e753" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,-4,-2⟩=8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127956/selection/6aefc878f4e148a160c6da2649ddb3eb48d683012291c090a4910a334a9fb4c7" :answer/id #uuid "1a3c2917-e957-5938-b145-2a4f805fb0bb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨2,-2,1⟩=15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127956/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "54bfcd08-ed0e-55e3-ad80-4da66ceab7db" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-127956/selection/6aefc878f4e148a160c6da2649ddb3eb48d683012291c090a4910a334a9fb4c7" :answer-field/choices ["q-127956/selection/4a259362c2a3e0418034bdb8a360ae2f2074603d64535d40483d48b2648fb2dc" "q-127956/selection/c4eb48c3cb07e7c3471776e0c89ba5f667a5d947317bec956bcc3c68bad1c1d9" "q-127956/selection/30cc1824d522d837a7d3dee93f22b9216bcf782fafd32ca5faf80f1b98e5500f" "q-127956/selection/6ce83711a830e5b9a0ac8b7db7cd2faa183875d3ab0d04a2213c2cfcda8d09ab" "q-127956/selection/6aefc878f4e148a160c6da2649ddb3eb48d683012291c090a4910a334a9fb4c7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-127956" :question/id #uuid "7d127c10-f6e2-5a96-ab28-c3201569ee57" :question/math-academy-id "q-127956" :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $Q(4,-2,3)$ and is  perpendicular to the line \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-1+2t \\\\ y=3-2t \\\\ z=5+t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vector of $Q$ is $q=⟨4,-2,3⟩.$ Converting the parametric equations of the line to vector form, we get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-1+2t \\\\ y=3-2t \\\\ z=5+t\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,⟨x,y,z⟩=⟨-1,3,5⟩+t\\text{ }{{⟨2,-2,1⟩}_{⏟}}_{v}.\n$$\n\n   \n\nThe direction vector of the line is $v=⟨2,-2,1⟩.$ So, a normal  vector to the plane is \n\n$$\nn=v=⟨2,-2,1⟩.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨2,-2,1⟩ & =⟨4,-2,3⟩\\cdot ⟨2,-2,1⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨2,-2,1⟩ & =15.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-127956/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "45cdbb0d-2986-5c05-8d23-dce29363051b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-127956"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-70894/selection/755bd4576dbe9ce02ddb52cfde411e40a9e76ad629430ebe2602da741f10f203" :answer/id #uuid "8f485774-81e4-5a79-8ff4-16967d44158f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,-1,2⟩=⟨2,1,-3⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70894/selection/04a905ad4a0f4ef7f228c830682c810620f85db68661511b14cc80ecaa879fd5" :answer/id #uuid "d60438d6-b5d2-5d15-a6df-28caf621fd6a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨2,1,3⟩=⟨1,-1,2⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70894/selection/dd7f5700348bc464a2f3e4b31c51a9f12c635461788d094a6bbc8a8039f5075b" :answer/id #uuid "9d342947-b3e8-545a-9175-0c68e2ab18bb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,-1,2⟩=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70894/selection/3778f3c6765ce880cd3abaea37ede23ef3da648c69c8bb74e3968ad3f072b750" :answer/id #uuid "1a565adb-24d5-50e4-bd12-79c885a09448" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨2,1,3⟩=-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70894/selection/b80e41666b51bea3a7b8b35f78177aa3fe4928f6e83a9bd66f9316713b67c973" :answer/id #uuid "6e428b4b-90f7-5cf9-9afd-0db57fee9352" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,-1,2⟩=-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70894/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "427df2f4-3901-5a58-af18-9a4b43dba7bb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-70894/selection/b80e41666b51bea3a7b8b35f78177aa3fe4928f6e83a9bd66f9316713b67c973" :answer-field/choices ["q-70894/selection/755bd4576dbe9ce02ddb52cfde411e40a9e76ad629430ebe2602da741f10f203" "q-70894/selection/04a905ad4a0f4ef7f228c830682c810620f85db68661511b14cc80ecaa879fd5" "q-70894/selection/dd7f5700348bc464a2f3e4b31c51a9f12c635461788d094a6bbc8a8039f5075b" "q-70894/selection/3778f3c6765ce880cd3abaea37ede23ef3da648c69c8bb74e3968ad3f072b750" "q-70894/selection/b80e41666b51bea3a7b8b35f78177aa3fe4928f6e83a9bd66f9316713b67c973"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-70894" :question/id #uuid "836af849-3232-5f71-9fa9-a73d0d879982" :question/math-academy-id "q-70894" :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $Q(2,1,-3)$ and is  perpendicular to the line \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=1+t \\\\ y=2-t \\\\ z=3+2t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vector of $Q$ is $q=⟨2,1,-3⟩.$ Converting the parametric equations of the line to vector form, we get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=1+t \\\\ y=2-t \\\\ z=3+2t\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,⟨x,y,z⟩=⟨1,2,3⟩+t\\text{ }{{⟨1,-1,2⟩}_{⏟}}_{v}.\n$$\n\n   \n\nThe direction vector of the line is $v=⟨1,-1,2⟩.$ So, a normal  vector to the plane is \n\n$$\nn=v=⟨1,-1,2⟩.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨1,-1,2⟩ & =⟨2,1,-3⟩\\cdot ⟨1,-1,2⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨1,-1,2⟩ & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-70894/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "45cdbb0d-2986-5c05-8d23-dce29363051b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-70894"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4932"] :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that contains the point $P(-3,2,1)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $\\mathbf{n}= \\langle 0, 2, 0 \\rangle.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is $\\mathbf{p}=\\langle -3,2,1 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{n}=\\langle 0,2,0 \\rangle$ is normal to the plane.\n\nThe equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(x_0,y_0,z_0)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $\\mathbf{n}$ can be given as\n\n$$\n(\\mathbf{r} - \\mathbf{p}) \\cdot \\mathbf{n} = 0,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf{r}$ is the position vector of any point on the plane, and $\\mathbf p$ is the position vector of $P.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-p\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨0,2,0⟩ & =⟨-3,2,1⟩\\cdot ⟨0,2,0⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨0,2,0⟩ & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4933"] :question/problem "A nonzero vector $\\langle 0,\\, \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{b}, \\: \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{c} \\rangle$ is parallel to the plane $\\mathbf{r} \\cdot \\langle 2, -1, 4 \\rangle  = 3.$ What is the value of $\\dfrac{b}{c}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need a vector $\\mathbf{v} = \\langle t_1,t_2,t_3 \\rangle$ that is parallel to the given plane. \n\nFrom the equation $\\mathbf{r} \\cdot \\langle 2, -1, 4 \\rangle  = 3$ of the plane, we get the normal vector $\\mathbf{n}=\\langle 2, -1, 4 \\rangle.$ So, $\\mathbf{v} \\perp \\mathbf{n}$ and we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ ⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩\\cdot ⟨2,-1,4⟩ & =0 \\\\ 2{t}_{1}-{t}_{2}+4{t}_{3} & =0 \\\\ {t}_{2} & =2{t}_{1}+4{t}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{v}=\\langle t_1, 2t_1 + 4t_3, t_3 \\rangle,\n$$\n\nwhere $t_1,t_3 \\in (-\\infty,\\infty).$ \n\nWe are told that the first component of $\\mathbf{v}$ equals $0.$ So, we must set $t_1=0.$ \n\nSince $\\mathbf{v}$ is nonzero, we can pick any $t_3 \\neq 0.$ For example, setting $t_3=1$, we get\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{v} = \\langle 0,\\, \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{4}, \\, \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{1} \\rangle.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\dfrac{b}{c} = 4.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4935"] :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $Q(\\sqrt{2},0,-5)$ and is perpendicular to the line\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=3 \\\\ y=-1+\\sqrt{3}t \\\\ z=5-t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vector of $Q$ is $\\mathbf{q}=\\langle \\sqrt{2},0,-5 \\rangle.$ Converting the parametric equations of the line to vector form, we get\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/assets/4c70e51d85874e5a241a5d9b35b147500d4c306187c5e0a1d15a48a9aef07706.png)\n\nThe direction vector of the line is $\\mathbf{v}=\\langle  0 , \\sqrt{3} , -1\\rangle,$ so a normal vector to the plane is \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{n}=\\mathbf{v}=\\langle  0 , \\sqrt{3} , -1 \\rangle.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨0,\\sqrt{3},-1⟩ & =⟨\\sqrt{2},0,-5⟩\\cdot ⟨0,\\sqrt{3},-1⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨0,\\sqrt{3},-1⟩ & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
